# Keep large and unused directories out of the Docker build context. The
# guest build copies only guest/, without guest/out/.
#
# guest/out/ must stay excluded. A plain host `make` builds .o files there with
# the musl cross-compiler; in the build context they make the container's
# `make shim` do nothing ("Nothing to be done"). The musl shim then ships
# instead of the glibc one, and every process that preloads it, EP122 included,
# dies with "libc.so: cannot open shared object file".
guest/out/
build/
dist/
target/
.git/
app/
tools/
initramfs-patch/
qemu/
crates/
docs/
